NAME
       sftp - copy files over SSH interactively

SYNOPSIS
       sftp [-P PORT] [-i KEYFILE] [USER@]HOST

DESCRIPTION
       sftp logs in to HOST through SSH and gives an sftp> prompt where you
       browse and copy files with short commands. It needs nothing on the
       server beyond sshd.

COMMANDS
       ls, cd, pwd
              List, change and show the remote directory.

       lls, lcd, lpwd
              The same for the local directory.

       get FILE [LOCAL]
              Download a file (get -r for a directory).

       put FILE [REMOTE]
              Upload a file (put -r for a directory).

       mkdir, rm, rename
              Change files on the server.

       bye, exit
              Leave.

EXAMPLES
           sftp student@server2
           sftp> put report.txt
           sftp> get /etc/motd
           sftp> bye

NOTES
       Cert Lab does not simulate sftp: use scp to copy files there.

SEE ALSO
       scp(1), ssh(1)
